{% render 'async-stylesheet', file: 'landing-founder.css' %}
<section class="founder">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="founder__inner">

            <div class="founder__profile">
                <div class="founder__info">
                    <div class="founder__photo">
                        <picture>
                            <source media="(max-width: 650px)" srcset="{{ 'founder-image-mobile.avif' | file_url }}"
                                type="image/avif">
                            <source media="(max-width: 650px)" srcset="{{ 'founder-image-mobile.webp' | file_url }}"
                                type="image/webp">
                            <source srcset="{{ 'founder-image.avif' | file_url }}" type="image/avif">
                            <img src="{{ 'founder-image.webp' | file_url }}" loading="lazy" alt="Alex — Founder of MYVOX-9"
                                width="604" height="668">
                        </picture>
                    </div>

                    <div class="founder__card">
                        <h3 class="founder__card-title">
                            Alex – Founder, MYVOX-9
                        </h3>

                        <p class="founder__card-text">
                            That bar is still how every batch ships today. <br>
                            If it doesn't clear it, it doesn't go out the door.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="founder__content">

                <header class="founder__header">
                    <h2 class="founder__title">
                        I Built Api-Complex <br> the Hard Way.
                        <span>On Purpose.</span>
                        <span>On Purpose</span>
                    </h2>

                    <p class="founder__subtitle">
                        I'm Alex, founder of MYVOX-9.
                    </p>
                </header>

                <div class="founder__intro">
                    <p>
                        A few years ago, I was the guy with a shelf full of supplements who still felt like
                        garbage.
                        And it wasn't just one thing going wrong. It was everything, a little:
                    </p>
                </div>

                <ul class="founder__problems">
                    <li class="founder__problem">
                        <svg>
                            <use href="#battery-icon"></use>
                        </svg>
                        <span>Energy that dropped out by 2 p.m.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li class="founder__problem">
                        <svg>
                            <use href="#brain-icon"></use>
                        </svg>
                        <span>Focus I had to claw for</span>
                    </li>

                    <li class="founder__problem">
                        <svg>
                            <use href="#fire-icon"></use>
                        </svg>
                        <span>A gut that made every meal a gamble</span>
                    </li>

                    <li class="founder__problem">
                        <svg>
                            <use href="#virus-icon"></use>
                        </svg>
                        <span>Feeling run-down whenever something went around</span>
                    </li>

                    <li class="founder__problem">
                        <svg>
                            <use href="#sad-icon"></use>
                        </svg>
                        <span>Just... running on empty</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <div class="founder__text">
                    <p>
                        So I did the responsible thing.<br>
                        I bought a bottle for each problem.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="founder__stats">

                    <article class="founder__stat">
                        <span class="founder__stat-value">6</span>
                        <span class="founder__stat-label">bottles</span>
                    </article>

                    <article class="founder__stat">
                        <span class="founder__stat-value">5</span>
                        <span class="founder__stat-label">alarms to remember them</span>
                    </article>

                    <article class="founder__stat">
                        <span class="founder__stat-value">$200+</span>
                        <span class="founder__stat-label">/mo</span>
                    </article>

                    <article class="founder__stat">
                        <span class="founder__stat-value">0</span>
                        <span class="founder__stat-label">real difference</span>
                    </article>

                </div>

                <blockquote class="founder__quote">
                    <svg>
                        <use href="#quote-icon"></use>
                    </svg>
                    <p>
                        In my early thirties. "Doing everything right." <br class="mobile-br">
                        And quietly deciding supplements just don't work.
                    </p>
                </blockquote>

                <div class="founder__story">

                    <p>
                        Here's what took me too long to see: I was treating five problems like five separate
                        fires.
                        But they weren't separate. They were one tired system, and nothing on that shelf was
                        built to support a system.
                        Six bottles, six directions, none of them talking to each other <br> or to me.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        So I went looking into what the body actually runs on — and the oldest answer there is
                        kept coming up:
                        the hive. Not one more single-ingredient bottle, but three substances that work as one
                        system —
                        building blocks, a signal, and a shield.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <blockquote class="founder__highlight">
                    <p>
                        The day it clicked, I wasn't chasing one fix anymore. <br>
                        Steadier energy, a clearer head, a calmer gut — it came up together.
                        <span>One stick had quietly replaced half my shelf, and I felt more like myself
                            than the whole drawer ever made me.</span>
                    </p>

                    <cite>— Alex</cite>
                </blockquote>

                <div class="founder__story">
                    <p>
                        So I went looking for a clean, full-dose version to buy for good. <br>
                        It didn't exist. Every label was the same story:
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="founder__comparison">

                    <article class="founder__comparison-card">
                        <picture>
                            <source srcset="{{ 'royal-jelly-image.avif' | file_url }}" type="image/avif">
                            <source srcset="{{ 'royal-jelly-image.webp' | file_url }}" type="image/webp">
                            <img src="{{ 'royal-jelly-image.webp' | file_url }}" alt="ROYAL JELLY" loading="lazy" width="84"
                                height="84">
                        </picture>

                        <div>
                            <h3>ROYAL JELLY</h3>
                            <p>drowned <br> in honey</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <article class="founder__comparison-card">
                        <picture>
                            <source srcset="{{ 'pollen-image.avif' | file_url }}" type="image/avif">
                            <source srcset="{{ 'pollen-image.webp' | file_url }}" type="image/webp">
                            <img src="{{ 'pollen-image.webp' | file_url }}" alt="POLLEN" loading="lazy" width="84"
                                height="84">
                        </picture>

                        <div>
                            <h3>POLLEN</h3>
                            <p>dosed so low the <br> number was decoration</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                </div>

                <div class="founder__text">
                    <p>
                        So I spent two years building the one I couldn't find. <br>
                        Here's the part that tells you who I am:
                    </p>
                </div>

                <article class="founder__principle">
                    <svg class="founder__principle-icon">
                        <use href="#heat-icon"></use>
                    </svg>

                    <div class="founder__principle-content">
                        <h3>
                            Royal jelly loses 10-HDA, its most fragile compound, <br>
                            the moment it gets warm.
                        </h3>

                        <p>
                            So I refused to let a single batch touch heat – even when <br>
                            it doubled my cost and three manufacturers told me it wasn't worth it.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <div class="founder__values">

                    <article class="founder__value">
                        <img src="{{ 'founder-icon-1.svg' | file_url }}" alt="Freeze-dried, never heated" loading="lazy">
                        <h3>Freeze-dried,<br>never <br> heated</h3>
                    </article>

                    <article class="founder__value">
                        <img src="{{ 'founder-icon-2.svg' | file_url }}" alt="Protected apiary sourced" loading="lazy">
                        <h3>Protected-<br>apiary sourced</h3>
                    </article>

                    <article class="founder__value">
                        <img src="{{ 'founder-icon-3.svg' | file_url }}" alt="No sugar,no flavoring, no filler"
                            loading="lazy">
                        <h3>No sugar,<br>no flavoring,<br class="mobile-br"><br>no filler</h3>
                    </article>

                    <article class="founder__value">
                        <img src="{{ 'founder-icon-4.svg' | file_url }}" alt="Three full doses,<br>one stick"
                            loading="lazy">
                        <h3>Three<br> full doses,<br>one <br class="mobile-br"> stick</h3>
                    </article>

                </div>

                <div class="founder__ending">
                    <p>
                        This isn't the cheapest bee supplement you can buy, and I've made peace with that.
                        I built the one stick I'd put in my own body every morning — so I could throw the rest
                        of the shelf out.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        I wouldn't give myself a watered-down version,
                        and I'm not going to give you one either.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>
